{"id": "opsc-mining-officer-2019-paper-2", "exam": "OPSC Geologist", "year": "2019 · Paper II (Applied Geology, Mining Officer)", "title": "OPSC Mining Officer 2019 — Paper II (Applied Geology)", "category": "Previous year paper", "description": "Official OPSC 2019 Paper II booklet for Mining Officer (Applied Geology), T.B.C. GGM-4/2019 — same recruitment cycle and syllabus family as the Geologist paper: 150 questions, 300 marks, 3 hours. Answer key prepared by Geo Scholars Academy. No negative marking in the 2019 paper; current pattern is +2 / −0.5.", "durationMinutes": 180, "sections": [{"name": "Paper", "from": 0, "to": 150}], "questions": [{"text": "Turbidity currents commonly deposit:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Shale", "Limestone", "Arkose", "Greywacke"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which kind of information can be determined from sedimentary structures?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Topping direction", "Means of transport of sediment", "Depositional environment", "All of these"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which type of cross bedding is a definite indicator of tidal environment?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Epsilon cross bedding", "Herringbone cross bedding", "Hummocky cross bedding", "Trough cross bedding"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Allochems in limestone consist of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Micrite only", "Spar only", "Ooids only", "Bioclasts and ooids"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following does not contain information about palaeocurrents?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Planar cross bedding", "Parting lineation", "Asymmetric ripples", "Laminar bedding"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The diameter of a sand grain is 1 mm. In phi (φ) grade, it is equivalent to:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["−1", "0", "1", "2"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Breccia and conglomerate differ in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Size of the clasts", "Shape of the clasts", "Cementing materials", "Environment of deposition"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following properties does not affect the permeability of sandstone?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Pore size", "Sorting", "Tortuosity of the pores", "Mineralogy of the framework grains"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "A salt dome is characterised by:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Low velocity and low density", "Low velocity and high density", "High velocity and high density", "High velocity and low density"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Rift valleys are bounded by:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Normal faults", "Reverse faults", "Strike slip faults", "Transform faults"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following sedimentary rocks indicates long distance transportation of the sediments?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Quartz sandstone", "Breccia", "Arkose (sandstone with lots of feldspar particles)", "None of these"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "______ is a well-sorted sandstone containing up to 75% quartz, with rock fragments in excess of feldspar.", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Arkose", "Lithic arenite", "Quartz arenite", "Feldspathic arenite"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Mud-supported limestone containing greater than 10% allochems is called:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Packstone", "Wackestone", "Grainstone", "Mudstone"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "A vertical sequence of rocks that changes from sandstone at the base through shale to limestone at the top of the sequence indicates a:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Transgression", "Regression", "Lagoonal environment", "Braided river"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Shale displays fissility because of the:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Recrystallisation of minerals", "Parallel arrangement of clay minerals", "Shearing", "Presence of mica plates"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Prior to compaction, deposits of sand in a quiet environment may have:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["20–30% volume open pore space", "80–90% volume open pore space", "40–50% volume open pore space", "60–70% volume open pore space"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Cubic packing of uniform size grains results in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["48% porosity", "26% porosity", "32% porosity", "65% porosity"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Coral reefs are generally found in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Polar regions", "Tropical regions", "Mid-latitude region", "Subtropical region"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Amongst the following rock types, we can expect best porosity in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Shaly siltstone", "Granular sandstone", "Medium grained sandstone", "Silty shale"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "In a rift basin, sandstones are likely to be:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Arkosic in composition", "Litharenitic in composition", "Quartz arenitic in composition", "Greywacke in composition"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The Siwalik basin is classified as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Back-arc basin", "Fore-arc basin", "Foreland basin", "Intracratonic basin"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Guano is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Calcareous deposit", "Phosphatic deposit", "Ferruginous deposit", "Siliceous deposit"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following methods is used for detailed exploration of oil and gas?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Gravity method", "Seismic refraction method", "Magnetic method", "Seismic reflection method"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Seismic survey is used in exploration most often to determine:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["The presence or absence of ore minerals associated with petroleum", "The presence or absence of a petroleum deposit", "Whether there are rock structures that could trap petroleum", "Whether there have been changes in petroleum deposits over time"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Reservoirs with grains that have the same size are called:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Well sorted", "Poorly sorted", "Half sorted", "Fully sorted"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The distribution of grain sizes within a reservoir refers to:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Compaction", "Sorting", "Packing", "Cementation"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Primary porosity is defined as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Pore space created by dissolution or fracturing of rock", "Pore space that is interconnected", "Pore space that is isolated or not interconnected", "Pore space created during deposition of sediments"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "For seismic S-wave velocity (V), the rigidity modulus (μ) is proportional to:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["√V", "V²", "V³", "V"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following logging techniques is best suited to estimate the shaliness of hydrocarbon reservoirs?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Resistivity", "Sonic", "Induction", "Gamma ray"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Choose the correct combination of the ore and location of its deposits:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Uranium – Jaduguda", "Lead – Khetri", "Gold – Panna", "Iron – Malanjkhand"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following varieties of limestone is entirely composed of organic matter?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Coquina", "Encrinite", "Spergenite", "Oolite"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following structures is that of Bombay High?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Doubly-plunging anticline", "Doubly-plunging syncline", "Non-plunging anticline", "Non-plunging syncline"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The polished and striated surface resulting due to friction along a fault plane is called:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Slickenside", "Lamination", "Ventifact", "None of these"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The resulting movement in a transcurrent fault is predominantly:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Vertical", "Horizontal", "Along the dip of fault", "Along the dip of bed"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The isotope ¹⁴C is produced in the earth's atmosphere by the interaction of cosmic rays with:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["¹⁶O resulting in release of α particles", "¹⁴N absorbing the neutron and releasing the proton", "¹⁰B resulting in the addition of two α particles", "¹³C absorbing a neutron"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Ratios of elemental abundances of the bulk earth are similar to that of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Moon", "Fe-Ni meteorites", "Chondrites", "Basaltic chondrites"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The space lattice structure of minerals is determined by:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Chemical analysis", "Scanning Electron Microscopy", "X-ray diffraction", "ICP-MS"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following represents the correct order of abundance of elements in the earth's crust?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Si > O > Fe > Al > Ca > Mg", "O > Al > Fe > Mg > Ca > Si", "O > Si > Fe > Mg > Ca > Al", "O > Si > Al > Fe > Mg > Ca"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Platinum Group Elements are:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Lithophile only", "Chalcophile only", "Siderophile only", "Both chalcophile and siderophile"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The wavelength range of the microwave region of electromagnetic radiation is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["0.4 to 0.7 µm", "1 mm to 1 m", "1.3 to 3 µm", "3 to 14 µm"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "GPS is used as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Gravity Profiling System", "Gas Prospective System", "Ground Penetrating System", "Geographic Location System"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "An igneous rock comprising predominantly of quartz and K-feldspar can be classified as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Gabbro", "Granite", "Peridotite", "Tonalite"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The surface expression of the lithosphere descending into the asthenosphere is known as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Island arc", "Benioff zone", "Canyon", "Trench"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following formations is rich in lignite with its correct stratigraphic age?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Palana Formation – Paleocene", "Disang Formation – Eocene", "Subathu Formation – Eocene", "Kopili Formation – Oligocene"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "In India, bituminous coals are found at:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Palana", "Neyveli", "Jharia", "Kutch"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Phosphorite deposits are found in which stratigraphic unit?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Udaipur Group", "Sausar Group", "Nallamalai Group", "Kaimur Group"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The disappearance of dinosaurs marks the end of which geological era?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Precambrian", "Cambrian", "Mesozoic", "Cenozoic"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The earthquakes with deep foci (~700 km) are common in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Mid-oceanic ridges", "Continental rifts", "Himalayan mountain belts", "Island arcs"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "'Ediacaran fossils' have significance in determining the:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Archaean/Proterozoic boundary", "Precambrian/Cambrian boundary", "Permian/Triassic boundary", "Cretaceous/Tertiary boundary"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Ammonoids are abundantly present in which of the following rock sequences?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Gondwana", "Cuddapah", "Jurassic of Kutch", "Siwalik"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Conversion of remains of plants and animals into rocks is known as:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Transformation", "Petrification", "Alteration", "Lithification"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The fossils which had short geological duration but wide geographical distribution are called:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Type fossils", "Rare fossils", "Index fossils", "Typical fossils"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Most faults in the Himalayas are:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Strike-slip", "Thrust", "Normal", "Transform"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following minerals in Mohs' scale of hardness is a silicate?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Topaz", "Apatite", "Fluorite", "Corundum"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Find the odd one out of the following:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Enstatite", "Hypersthene", "Anthophyllite", "Diopside"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Tetrahedral structure of a silicate mineral develops Si : O ratio of 4 : 11. The silicate structure of the mineral is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Nesosilicate", "Inosilicate", "Tectosilicate", "Sorosilicate"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Find the odd one out of the following pairs:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Aragonite – Calcite", "Diamond – Graphite", "Quartz – Chalcedony", "Microcline – Labradorite"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Mesozoic–Cenozoic boundary is placed at:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["75 Ma", "65 Ma", "45 Ma", "110 Ma"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "A line on a map connecting points of equal elevation is called:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Map line", "Base line", "Contour line", "Isotherm"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "In which of the following regions is the thickness of the crust maximum?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Continental rifts", "Mid-oceanic ridges", "Orogenic belts", "Passive margins"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Reverse faults are responsible for:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Lengthening of the strata", "Shortening of the strata", "Overturning of the strata", "Thinning of the strata"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "If the heave of a fault is zero, then the fault is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["High angle fault", "Low angle fault", "Horizontal fault", "Vertical fault"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Taking a photograph of an object on a clear bright day is an example of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Active remote sensing", "Passive remote sensing", "Microwave remote sensing", "Thermal remote sensing"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which one of the following was the first Indian Remote Sensing Satellite?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Rohini", "IRS-1A", "Bhaskara-1", "Cartosat"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which one of the following methods is used for dating recent geological events?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["²³⁵U – ²⁰⁶Pb", "¹⁴C", "⁴⁰K – ⁴⁰Ar", "⁸⁷Rb – ⁸⁷Sr"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following is the ore of tungsten?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Psilomelane", "Azurite", "Scheelite", "Pyrite"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The petroleum deposits of Digboi oil field occur in the rock formation of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Miocene age", "Oligocene age", "Eocene age", "Jurassic age"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Fault line, railway line and roads are best represented in GIS by:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["TIN models", "Raster data models", "Vector data models", "Georelational data models"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Geiger–Müller counter is commonly used for the exploration of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Uranium deposits", "Bauxite deposits", "Iron ore deposits", "Copper ore deposits"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "How many silicate minerals are there in Mohs' scale of hardness?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["7", "5", "3", "4"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which one is the main constituent of the gas form of petroleum?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Propane", "Butane", "Methane", "Ethene"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following minerals is most resistant to weathering?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Muscovite", "Biotite", "Calcite", "Quartz"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Twinning observed in plagioclase:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Carlsbad twinning", "Polysynthetic twinning", "Penetration twinning", "Cross-hatch twinning"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which mineral is used for the age determination of the Vindhyan Sandstone?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Quartz", "Pyrite", "Glauconite", "Ilmenite"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "'Smith test' is used to determine which of the following properties of a building stone?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Density", "Porosity", "Durability", "Permeability"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following is a geostationary satellite?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Landsat", "INSAT", "SPOT", "IRS"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The graphite deposits of Odisha are associated with:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Granite", "Basic granulite", "Charnockite", "Khondalite"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Manganese deposits of Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra belt are associated with rocks of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Sakoli Group", "Mahakoshal Group", "Bababudan Group", "Sausar Group"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The volcanic equivalent of diorite is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Rhyolite", "Andesite", "Trachyte", "Basalt"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "If the colour of gossan is black, it indicates the presence of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Copper", "Iron", "Manganese", "Graphite"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Heavy minerals are those which have specific gravity of more than:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["3.52", "2.87", "3.00", "3.87"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The bauxite of the East-coast bauxite deposit is formed from rock like:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Granite", "Basalt", "Khondalite", "Charnockite"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following formations contains asbestos deposits in Andhra Pradesh?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Gulcheru", "Vempalle", "Cumbum", "Bairenkonda"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Maximum separation of the reflectance values of vegetation, soil and water is seen in:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Green band", "Red band", "Infrared band", "Blue band"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Bauxite is a:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Residual deposit", "Chemical deposit", "Transported deposit", "Ferruginous deposit"], "answer": 0, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Fuel ratio of a coal is defined by:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Organic sulphur / Organic phosphorus", "Moisture / Volatile matter", "Volatile matter / Ash content", "Fixed carbon / Volatile matter"], "answer": 3, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Spatial resolution of the passive sensors depends on their:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["GPS", "FOV", "IFOV", "Pixel"], "answer": 2, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Which of the following data gives maximum vertical accuracy?", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["RADAR", "LiDAR", "Thermal image", "Microwave"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "Kimberlite indicates the possibility of the presence of:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Ruby", "Diamond", "Kyanite", "Sapphire"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "The primary source of energy that moves heat and water through the hydrosphere and atmosphere is:", "type": "mcq", "solution": "", "options": ["Wind energy", "Solar energy", "Heat energy released from the earth", "None of these"], "answer": 1, "marks": 2, "negative": 0}, {"text": "What percentage of earth's 